### How to write the declaration

The notebook shows that the spaces do not matter. These three lines all declare a pointer to `int`:

```c
int *ptr1;
int* ptr2;
int * ptr3;
```

The course writes `int *ptr`, with the `*` next to the name. There is a reason, shown in the next pitfall.

